cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Rootline, please cite it as below."
title: "Rootline: an open benchmark and replay app for evidence-grounded AI diagnosis of microservice failures"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: flotrpy
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Flotrpy/RootLine"
abstract: >-
  Rootline is an open, reproducible benchmark and replay app for
  evidence-grounded AI diagnosis of microservice failures. It measures which
  telemetry signals free and open models need and whether they can tell
  network faults from application faults (v0.1), with real Wi-Fi faults on
  two Arduino UNO Q boards next to their emulated counterparts.
keywords:
  - root cause analysis
  - observability
  - OpenTelemetry
  - large language models
  - benchmark
